ae2s_ponder.gui.drive.title=ME Drive: insert storage
ae2s_ponder.gui.drive.target.slot.STORAGE_CELL.0=Storage cell slot
ae2s_ponder.gui.drive.target.slot.STORAGE_CELL.1=Additional cell
ae2s_ponder.gui.drive.step.0=Insert an ME storage cell. The drive needs network power and a channel before the terminal can use it.
ae2s_ponder.gui.drive.step.1=The ten slots hold independent cells. Add a larger cell when bytes or available types run short.
ae2s_ponder.gui.drive.step.2=Cell contents stay on the cell when you remove it. Keep a backup before reorganizing your storage.
ae2s_ponder.gui.drive.step.3=Close this window and open the ME Terminal to test insertion and extraction. A drive is not a direct item input.
ae2s_ponder.gui.terminal.title=ME Terminal: search and transfer
ae2s_ponder.gui.terminal.target.widget.search=Search
ae2s_ponder.gui.terminal.target.repo.0=Network stock
ae2s_ponder.gui.terminal.target.slot.PLAYER_INVENTORY.0=Player inventory
ae2s_ponder.gui.terminal.step.0=Click the search box and enter part of an item name. While typing, W stays available as a search character; click outside before holding W for guidance.
ae2s_ponder.gui.terminal.step.1=The item grid shows this network's stored and craftable entries. Click a stocked item to take it; craftable entries can start a request.
ae2s_ponder.gui.terminal.step.2=Transfer items between your inventory and network storage. The demonstration uses separate items and does not move your real inventory.
ae2s_ponder.gui.terminal.step.3=Clear the search to see everything again. If the terminal is offline, check power, cable connections, channels and loaded chunks.
ae2s_ponder.gui.cell_workbench.title=Cell Workbench: configure a partition
ae2s_ponder.gui.cell_workbench.target.slot.STORAGE_CELL.0=Cell to configure
ae2s_ponder.gui.cell_workbench.target.slot.CONFIG.0=Partition filter
ae2s_ponder.gui.cell_workbench.step.0=Insert the storage cell you want to configure. Read its current contents before changing restrictions.
ae2s_ponder.gui.cell_workbench.step.1=Set the item filters in the configuration grid. These are ghost entries; they select allowed types and do not supply stored items.
ae2s_ponder.gui.cell_workbench.step.2=Use supported cell upgrades only when needed. Page buttons appear for cells with more filter entries; live highlights follow the visible slots.
ae2s_ponder.gui.cell_workbench.step.3=Remove the configured cell and put it back into the drive. Confirm that allowed items enter it and other types use a different cell.
ae2s_ponder.gui.inscriber.title=Inscriber: print a silicon circuit
ae2s_ponder.gui.inscriber.target.slot.INSCRIBER_PLATE_TOP.0=Upper press slot
ae2s_ponder.gui.inscriber.target.slot.INSCRIBER_PLATE_BOTTOM.0=Lower press slot
