ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_crafting.step.1=Insert a blank pattern. The guide observes this real slot and never places an item for you.
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_crafting.step.2=Fill the recipe grid and verify the resulting item. These are recipe entries; ingredients are supplied when a crafting request executes.
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_crafting.step.3=Click Encode after checking mode, ingredients and output. Encoding still requires a valid recipe and a blank pattern.
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_crafting.step.4=Take the encoded pattern and install it in a Pattern Provider beside a Molecular Assembler; the network also needs a Crafting CPU.
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_processing.title=Pattern Terminal: processing
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_processing.target.widget.modeTabButton1=Processing mode
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_processing.target.slot.BLANK_PATTERN.0=Blank pattern
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_processing.target.slot.PROCESSING_INPUTS.0=Consumed material
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_processing.target.slot.PROCESSING_OUTPUTS.0=Expected product
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_processing.target.widget.encodePattern=Encode
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_processing.target.slot.ENCODED_PATTERN.0=Encoded pattern
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_processing.step.0=Choose Processing for an external machine recipe.
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_processing.step.1=Insert a blank pattern. The guide observes this real slot and never places an item for you.
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_processing.step.2=Specify exactly the consumed inputs and expected outputs. Keep reusable presses installed in the machine; do not list them as consumed ingredients.
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_processing.step.3=Click Encode after checking mode, ingredients and output. Encoding still requires a valid recipe and a blank pattern.
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_processing.step.4=Take the encoded pattern and install it in a Pattern Provider. Processing outputs must return to the same requesting network.
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_provider.title=Pattern Provider: install and return
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_provider.target.slot.ENCODED_PATTERN.0=Encoded patterns
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_provider.target.slot.STORAGE.0=Return buffer
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_provider.target.widget.openPriority=Priority
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_provider.step.0=Insert a matching encoded pattern. A crafting pattern uses a Molecular Assembler; a processing pattern delivers ingredients to the adjacent machine.
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_provider.step.1=The return buffer receives products for the network. A separate Import Bus can also return products to the same network.
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_provider.step.2=Set priority only when several providers offer the recipe. Check target orientation and blocking mode before increasing parallel work.
ae2s_ponder.gui.pattern_provider.step.3=Request one batch and confirm the exact product returns. The task waits until the requesting network receives it.
ae2s_ponder.gui.interface.title=ME Interface: stock and insert
ae2s_ponder.gui.interface.target.slot.CONFIG.0=Requested stock
ae2s_ponder.gui.interface.target.slot.STORAGE.0=Local inventory
ae2s_ponder.gui.interface.step.0=Configure the desired item and amount in a ghost slot. This entry requests stock; it is not an already supplied item.
ae2s_ponder.gui.interface.step.1=With network power, a channel and enough stored items, the interface replenishes its real local inventory.
ae2s_ponder.gui.interface.step.2=Let the adjacent machine consume from the real inventory. Avoid routing those same items straight back into the interface.
ae2s_ponder.gui.interface.step.3=An interface can accept machine output into network storage. Use a Pattern Provider for processing-pattern ingredient delivery.
ae2s_ponder.gui.me_chest.title=ME Chest: local storage
ae2s_ponder.gui.me_chest.target.slot.STORAGE_CELL.0=Storage cell
ae2s_ponder.gui.me_chest.step.0=Install one compatible cell. The ME Chest has a cell slot, rather than the ten-cell capacity of a drive.
ae2s_ponder.gui.me_chest.target.view.body=Power and access
ae2s_ponder.gui.me_chest.step.1=Supply power, then use the storage access button to browse the installed cell. Check access restrictions if insertion fails.
ae2s_ponder.gui.me_chest.step.2=The contents remain on the removed cell. Before replacing it, finish any active transfer and keep the original cell safe.
ae2s_ponder.gui.sky_chest.title=Sky Stone Chest
ae2s_ponder.gui.sky_chest.target.slot.STORAGE.0=Chest inventory
ae2s_ponder.gui.sky_chest.step.0=These are real chest slots. Place and retrieve items here; this chest does not require an ME network.
ae2s_ponder.gui.sky_chest.target.slot.PLAYER_INVENTORY.0=Transfer items
ae2s_ponder.gui.sky_chest.step.1=Move items between the chest and your inventory. Demonstration items are independent of the real inventory.
ae2s_ponder.gui.sky_chest.step.2=Attach a Storage Bus to expose this inventory to ME storage. Configure access and priority on the bus itself.
ae2s_ponder.gui.io_port.title=ME IO Port: transfer cells
ae2s_ponder.gui.io_port.target.slot.MACHINE_INPUT.0=Input cells
ae2s_ponder.gui.io_port.step.0=Insert storage cells to be processed. Their contents, not ordinary loose items, are transferred by this machine.
ae2s_ponder.gui.io_port.target.widget.operationMode=Transfer direction
ae2s_ponder.gui.io_port.step.1=Choose cell-to-network or network-to-cell before starting. Check that the destination accepts the stored resource types.
ae2s_ponder.gui.io_port.target.slot.MACHINE_OUTPUT.0=Completed cells
ae2s_ponder.gui.io_port.step.2=Completed cells move to the output side. The selected completion rule decides when a cell counts as finished.
ae2s_ponder.gui.io_port.target.widget.upgrades=Throughput and stalls
ae2s_ponder.gui.io_port.step.3=Use supported upgrades after testing one cell. A full network, restrictive partition or wrong direction can stop transfers.
ae2s_ponder.gui.condenser.title=Condenser: matter and singularities
ae2s_ponder.gui.condenser.target.slot.MACHINE_INPUT.0=Consumed resources
ae2s_ponder.gui.condenser.step.0=Only feed resources you intend to consume. This machine converts supplied resources into accumulated matter.
ae2s_ponder.gui.condenser.target.widget.mode=Output mode
ae2s_ponder.gui.condenser.step.1=Choose deletion, Matter Ball or Singularity mode as appropriate. Read the displayed requirement before feeding valuables.
ae2s_ponder.gui.condenser.target.slot.STORAGE_CELL.0=Matter capacity
ae2s_ponder.gui.condenser.step.2=Install a compatible storage component when the chosen output requires accumulated capacity.
ae2s_ponder.gui.condenser.target.slot.MACHINE_OUTPUT.0=Collect the product
ae2s_ponder.gui.condenser.step.3=Keep the output clear. A Singularity still needs the actual entangling recipe before it can pair two quantum bridges.
ae2s_ponder.gui.vibration_chamber.title=Vibration Chamber: generate power
ae2s_ponder.gui.vibration_chamber.target.slot.MACHINE_INPUT.0=Fuel
ae2s_ponder.gui.vibration_chamber.step.0=Insert a valid furnace fuel. Fuel is consumed to supply AE power to the connected network.
ae2s_ponder.gui.vibration_chamber.target.widget.generationRateBar=Generation
ae2s_ponder.gui.vibration_chamber.step.1=Watch generation and demand. An Energy Cell stores surplus energy; it does not generate energy by itself.
ae2s_ponder.gui.vibration_chamber.target.widget.upgrades=Upgrades and supply
ae2s_ponder.gui.vibration_chamber.step.2=Use only upgrades supported by this machine. Automate fuel supply separately and test that the network stays powered under load.
ae2s_ponder.gui.crystal_assembler.title=Crystal Assembler
ae2s_ponder.gui.crystal_assembler.target.slot.MACHINE_INPUT.0=Recipe input
ae2s_ponder.gui.crystal_assembler.step.0=Look up the installed Crystal Assembler recipe, then supply its input here. Do not assume a modern AE2 recipe applies unchanged.
ae2s_ponder.gui.crystal_assembler.target.slot.STORAGE.0=Supporting inventory
ae2s_ponder.gui.crystal_assembler.step.1=Check the recipe and the machine tooltip for the role of these supporting slots before automating them.
ae2s_ponder.gui.crystal_assembler.target.widget.progressBar=Powered processing
ae2s_ponder.gui.crystal_assembler.step.2=Connect power and watch progress. When processing stalls, check the complete recipe, available power and output space.
ae2s_ponder.gui.crystal_assembler.target.slot.MACHINE_OUTPUT.0=Return products
ae2s_ponder.gui.crystal_assembler.step.3=Extract only the intended product and return it to the requesting network when using a processing pattern.
ae2s_ponder.gui.ingredient_buffer.title=Ingredient Buffer
ae2s_ponder.gui.ingredient_buffer.target.slot.STORAGE.0=Ingredient inventory
ae2s_ponder.gui.ingredient_buffer.step.0=Use the buffer as an intermediate inventory between delivery and the processing machine.
ae2s_ponder.gui.ingredient_buffer.target.slot.STORAGE.1=Keep batches traceable
ae2s_ponder.gui.ingredient_buffer.step.1=Test one batch and verify which adjacent side inserts and extracts. A buffer does not turn an incorrect pattern into a valid recipe.
ae2s_ponder.gui.ingredient_buffer.step.2=Keep product return separate from ingredient delivery so the crafting CPU receives the expected output.
ae2s_ponder.gui.caner.title=ME Caner: container transfer
ae2s_ponder.gui.caner.target.slot.CANER_CONTAINER.0=Container
ae2s_ponder.gui.caner.step.0=Place a compatible fillable or filled container here. Check its supported resource and capacity.
ae2s_ponder.gui.caner.target.slot.CANER_CONTENT.0=Contents
ae2s_ponder.gui.caner.step.1=Inspect the resource entry handled by the Caner. Choose the intended fill or empty operation using its native controls.
ae2s_ponder.gui.caner.step.2=Test one container before connecting automation. Ensure both the container destination and resource destination have space.
ae2s_ponder.gui.molecular_assembler.title=Molecular Assembler
ae2s_ponder.gui.molecular_assembler.target.slot.ENCODED_PATTERN.0=Crafting patterns
ae2s_ponder.gui.molecular_assembler.step.0=Use crafting patterns for crafting-grid recipes. Processing patterns belong to machines that perform the described process.
ae2s_ponder.gui.molecular_assembler.target.widget.upgrades=Acceleration
ae2s_ponder.gui.molecular_assembler.step.1=Install supported acceleration upgrades after a single recipe works. Parallel demand also depends on the available crafting CPUs and ingredient supply.
ae2s_ponder.gui.molecular_assembler.step.2=A neighboring Pattern Provider can send crafting work to an assembler. Check adjacency and network power when a job waits.
ae2s_ponder.gui.molecular_assembler.target.widget.openPriority=Duplicate recipes
ae2s_ponder.gui.molecular_assembler.step.3=If several devices offer the same recipe, inspect their priority and availability before scaling the setup.
ae2s_ponder.gui.import_bus.title=Import Bus
ae2s_ponder.gui.import_bus.target.slot.CONFIG.0=Resource filter
ae2s_ponder.gui.import_bus.step.0=Pull items from the adjacent inventory into ME storage. The target is the inventory on the bus face.
ae2s_ponder.gui.import_bus.target.widget.verticalToolbar=Operation settings
ae2s_ponder.gui.import_bus.step.1=Read the supported redstone, matching, scheduling and access settings. Availability depends on this bus and installed cards.
ae2s_ponder.gui.import_bus.target.widget.upgrades=Upgrade cards
ae2s_ponder.gui.import_bus.step.2=Install only compatible cards. Extra filter slots can remain disabled until the required capacity upgrade is present.
ae2s_ponder.gui.import_bus.step.3=Use a small amount to confirm direction, free destination space and network power. Avoid a direct import/export loop on the same inventory.
