ae2s_ponder.gui.stock_amount.step.0=Enter the desired local amount and check its unit and maximum. Zero can have a special clearing or disabling meaning on the parent device.
ae2s_ponder.gui.stock_amount.target.widget.save=Save the target
ae2s_ponder.gui.stock_amount.step.1=Save only after confirming the intended resource. The amount is a target, not a supplied inventory stack.
ae2s_ponder.gui.stock_amount.target.widget.back=Return to the device
ae2s_ponder.gui.stock_amount.step.2=Inspect the parent configuration and test actual replenishment after changing a target.
ae2s_ponder.gui.wireless_access_point.title=Wireless Access Point: pair a device
ae2s_ponder.gui.wireless_access_point.target.slot.MACHINE_INPUT.0=Device to pair
ae2s_ponder.gui.wireless_access_point.step.0=Insert a supported wireless device into the pairing input. This associates the device with this network access point.
ae2s_ponder.gui.wireless_access_point.target.slot.MACHINE_OUTPUT.0=Paired device
ae2s_ponder.gui.wireless_access_point.step.1=Collect the paired device from the output. Keep it charged before trying remote access.
ae2s_ponder.gui.wireless_access_point.target.text.range=Wireless range
ae2s_ponder.gui.wireless_access_point.step.2=Read the actual range and energy use. Supported booster slots can change the tradeoff between range and power cost.
ae2s_ponder.gui.wireless_access_point.target.slot.STORAGE.0=Boosters and testing
ae2s_ponder.gui.wireless_access_point.step.3=Use compatible boosters, then test access from the intended location and dimension. Do not assume every wireless feature bypasses range.
ae2s_ponder.gui.quantum_bridge.title=Quantum Bridge: pair the ends
ae2s_ponder.gui.quantum_bridge.target.slot.STORAGE.0=Entangled pair
ae2s_ponder.gui.quantum_bridge.step.0=Place one member of the same entangled pair into each completed bridge. An ordinary Singularity is not an already paired entangled item.
ae2s_ponder.gui.quantum_bridge.target.view.body=Power and formation
ae2s_ponder.gui.quantum_bridge.step.1=Check the full ring structure and power on both ends. Merely inserting the pair does not repair an incomplete structure.
ae2s_ponder.gui.quantum_bridge.step.2=Keep relevant chunks loaded and test the intended remote device. Removing the paired item disconnects the link.
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_io.title=Spatial IO Port: transfer a region
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_io.target.slot.MACHINE_INPUT.0=Spatial cell
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_io.step.0=Insert a Spatial Storage Cell large enough for the defined region. It stores a spatial region rather than ordinary item stacks.
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_io.target.text.scs_size=Defined region
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_io.step.1=Verify the displayed spatial dimensions against the Spatial Pylon setup before operating the port.
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_io.target.text.required_power=Energy and efficiency
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_io.step.2=Read required energy, available energy and efficiency. The network must have enough stored energy for the transfer.
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_io.target.slot.MACHINE_OUTPUT.0=Complete and recover
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_io.step.3=Trigger the port using the intended control and collect the resulting cell. Test with a small nonvaluable region first.
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_anchor.title=Spatial Anchor: loaded chunks
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_anchor.target.text.loaded_chunks=Loaded chunks
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_anchor.step.0=Inspect the loaded chunk count and the network area affected by this anchor.
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_anchor.target.text.used_power=Power cost
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_anchor.step.1=Read the ongoing power cost. Keep the network powered if its operation depends on loaded chunks.
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_anchor.target.widget.verticalToolbar=Overlay and verification
ae2s_ponder.gui.spatial_anchor.step.2=Use the supported overlay to inspect coverage, then verify the actual remote machines keep operating.
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_status.title=Network status: power and channels
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_status.target.text.stored_power=Stored energy
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_status.step.0=Compare current energy with capacity. A nonzero battery does not guarantee generation will keep up with demand.
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_status.target.text.power_usage_rate=Energy demand
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_status.step.1=Compare input, usage and channel-related energy demand to find a power deficit.
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_status.target.widget.scrollbar=Connected devices
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_status.step.2=Scroll the device overview and check that expected machines appear in the correct network.
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_status.target.text.channel_power_rate=Channel checks
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_status.step.3=When a machine is offline, also check cable capacity, controller topology and loaded chunks; energy alone is not enough.
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_tool.title=Network Tool: upgrades and diagnostics
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_tool.target.slot.STORAGE.0=Upgrade storage
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_tool.step.0=Keep compatible upgrade cards in the tool inventory for maintenance. These are real stored cards.
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_tool.target.view.body=Inspect the target network
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_tool.step.1=Use the tool on the intended network device to inspect its actual status. Verify which network you are examining.
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_tool.step.2=Keep room for removed cards and verify the machine settings after changing upgrades.
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_analyser.title=Network Analyzer
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_analyser.target.text.mode_value=Analysis mode
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_analyser.step.0=Choose the intended display mode and inspect which nodes or connections it classifies.
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_analyser.target.text.normal_nodes=Node statistics
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_analyser.step.1=Compare normal, dense and missing node statistics. The labels describe the current analysis, not automatic repairs.
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_analyser.target.widget.color_window=Overlay colors
ae2s_ponder.gui.network_analyser.step.2=Configure distinguishable colors, then inspect the world overlay to locate the corresponding cables and devices.
ae2s_ponder.gui.tick_analyser.title=Tick Analyzer
ae2s_ponder.gui.tick_analyser.target.widget.duration_input=Sample duration
ae2s_ponder.gui.tick_analyser.step.0=Set a sampling duration long enough to observe a representative machine cycle.
ae2s_ponder.gui.tick_analyser.target.view.body=Read the distribution
ae2s_ponder.gui.tick_analyser.step.1=Compare sampled work rather than drawing conclusions from one spike. Inspect the selected target and analysis range.
ae2s_ponder.gui.tick_analyser.target.text.range_1=Compare under the same load
ae2s_ponder.gui.tick_analyser.step.2=Repeat a sample under the same workload after a change so the result has a useful comparison.
ae2s_ponder.gui.advanced_memory_card.title=Advanced Memory Card: P2P management
ae2s_ponder.gui.advanced_memory_card.target.widget.search=Find a tunnel
ae2s_ponder.gui.advanced_memory_card.step.0=Search tunnel entries by the available identifying information. Give endpoints names before managing a large installation.
ae2s_ponder.gui.advanced_memory_card.target.view.body=Roles and frequency
ae2s_ponder.gui.advanced_memory_card.step.1=Inspect each entry's type, input/output role, frequency and location before binding.
ae2s_ponder.gui.advanced_memory_card.target.widget.scrollbar=Select the intended endpoint
ae2s_ponder.gui.advanced_memory_card.step.2=Scroll to the intended endpoint and use the native bind action deliberately. Pair compatible tunnel types and keep the carrier powered.
ae2s_ponder.gui.advanced_memory_card.step.3=Test the actual remote device after binding. A saved entry is not proof that its current world position is loaded and online.
ae2s_ponder.gui.cell_restriction.title=Storage cell restrictions
ae2s_ponder.gui.cell_restriction.target.widget.amountInput=Amount limit
ae2s_ponder.gui.cell_restriction.step.0=Set the amount limit supported by the selected cell. Check whether you intend a restrictive cap before applying it.
ae2s_ponder.gui.cell_restriction.target.widget.typesInput=Type limit
ae2s_ponder.gui.cell_restriction.step.1=Set the allowed number of resource types without confusing types with stored item count.
ae2s_ponder.gui.cell_restriction.target.widget.set=Apply restrictions
ae2s_ponder.gui.cell_restriction.step.2=Apply only to the intended cell, then inspect the cell tooltip and test one insertion.
ae2s_ponder.gui.cell_restriction.target.widget.release=Release restrictions
